OPINION VERSUS FACT. This work is a survey of strategies, mechanisms,
and research findings drawn from published books, public video
instruction, and peer-reviewed financial research. Where the author
attributes a strategy, claim, or argument to a named third party,
that attribution reflects a good-faith characterization of that party's
publicly stated position, drawn from publicly available source material,
and is not intended to misrepresent or defame any party. Sections
marked "Reconstruction" contain the book's own conjecture about
underlying mechanisms and should be read as analytical interpretation,
not as statements of fact or as positions held by any cited source.
Where the text contains editorial judgment, the judgment is the
author's alone and reflects his interpretation of the source material
rather than any independent finding of fact.

NO ENDORSEMENT IMPLIED. No author, researcher, practitioner, publisher,
fund, organization, or institution mentioned in this work has endorsed,
authorized, reviewed, sponsored, or otherwise associated themselves
with the work, except where explicitly stated. Mention of any person
or organization is not an endorsement of this work by that party, nor
is it an endorsement of that party by the author.

AI-ASSISTED AUTHORSHIP. The chapters in this book were drafted by
Claude, an artificial intelligence language model produced by
Anthropic, PBC, working against an indexed source corpus under
detailed instructions from the author. The author selected the
sources, designed the chapter structure, set the editorial framing,
and made all decisions about what to include and exclude. The AI
performed the drafting, cross-referencing, and citation against the
corpus. No fact-checking outside the corpus was performed.
Verifiability is bounded by the corpus. Readers who object to
AI-assisted writing on principle are advised that this work is
unsuitable for them.

HYPOTHETICAL AND BACKTESTED PERFORMANCE. Where the book reports
backtested returns, simulated results, or historical strategy
performance, these figures are drawn from published sources and
are subject to all the limitations those sources disclose: data-
